### 38 cli query --help
$ xmd query --help --root <root> --now 2026-09-16T12:00:00-04:00
exit 0
--- stdout
Query tasks, values, tables, plans, resources and diagnostics

Usage: xmd query [OPTIONS] <QUERY>                (note on stdin)
       xmd query [OPTIONS] <FILE> <QUERY>
       xmd query [OPTIONS] --workspace <QUERY>

Arguments:
  [FILE_OR_QUERY]  A note relative to --root, or the query itself when the note is piped in or --workspace is set
  [QUERY]          An expression over the workspace's collections; use - for stdin

Options:
      --workspace      Query all indexed notes instead of supplying a positional note file
      --root <ROOT>    [default: .]
      --json           Emit a JSON array, preserving dates, currencies and units
      --jsonl          Emit one JSON value per line
      --on <ON>        Evaluate at local midnight on this date
      --now <NOW>      Freeze the clock and timezone offset using an RFC3339 timestamp
      --fail-on-match  Return exit status 1 if the query returns any rows (useful for diagnostics)
  -h, --help           Print help

Bindings: ast, graph, days, timers, mentions, links, tasks, checkboxes, events, stops, entries, values, forms, plans, decisions, tables, rows, resources, diagnostics, notes, sections, calculations, references, cells, recognized, attributed
Functions: map, filter, fold, get, sort_by, desc, group_by, slice, concat, sum, length
xs | f(a) is f(xs, a); .due is fn(x) => x.due; .{title, due} picks fields.
Use - as QUERY to read an expression from stdin; the note then has to be a file.
Examples: xmd query note.x.md 'tasks | sort_by(desc(.due)) | map(.title)' --json
          cat note.x.md | xmd query 'tasks | length'
          xmd query --workspace 'filter(tasks, fn(t) => !t.done)' --json
          printf 'length(tasks)' | xmd query note.x.md -

